      "message": "By replacing `test` with `test_gcc` and `test_llvm` here, the default `make test` target will no longer run `zmake_unit_tests` and `test_host_utils`. Because of this, if you run a default coverage build (`COVERAGE\u003d1`), these two targets won\u0027t run at all since the `test` target doesn\u0027t depend on them anymore.\n\nA clean way to fix this and simplify the Makefile is to just add:\n```make\ntest: test_gcc test_llvm\n```\nIf you add this, `test` will transitively depend on all the necessary targets. This means you could also delete the `test: $(COVERAGE_TARGETS)` line below and the `test: twister_host twister_llvm ...` line in the `else` block.",
